You can set the date to 31-DEC-1999 23:59. After that
you need one minute of your lifetime and ULTRIX is in y2k.
You have to repeat this for every year after y2k of course,
but 2004 isn't that far away from 1999 ;-)
This procedure works with about any Unix system and
in most cases that's enough. The Y2K patches include
a patched libc too IIRC, but if you just care that
the date is set correctly then you are fine.

